er Education (MOHE) through the Fundamental Research Grant Scheme (FRGS) under Grant FRGS/1/2023/TK07/UITM/02/22; and in part by the Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Universiti Teknologi MARA, Shah Alam, Selangor, Malaysia. ABSTRACT Dynamic Thermal Rating (DTR) offers a flexible and adaptive solution to overcome the limitations of static thermal rating in power transmission. This systematic review aims to map and analyze the current state of research on DTR, specifically focusing on underground cable systems. The review contributes to a clearer understanding of DTR’s role in improving the efficiency and resilience of underground cable networks, while also laying the groundwork for future studies to address current limitations. The novelty of this paper lies in its structured synthesis that links modeling techni"
